# rules: swift-webview-loads-untrusted-url
# languages: swift
# fixture: swift/CWE-601.swift
# from: CWE-601 (Open Redirect), CWE-749, MASVS-PLATFORM-3
#
# An app that registers a URL scheme or a universal link accepts a URL from any
# other app on the phone and from any web page the user taps. Handing part of
# that URL to a web view means whoever sent it chooses the page, and the page
# then renders inside the app's own chrome: sharing the web view's cookies,
# beside its script message handlers, and behind whatever the user believes the
# app to be. That last part is the reason this is worth reporting even where
# the web view has no bridge on it - the address bar the user would check is
# not there.
#
# The fix is an allowlist of hosts compared after the URL is parsed, and there
# is no way to spell a comparison as a sanitizer: a sanitizer stops a flow by
# covering one of its ends, and `parsed.host == "app.example.com"` sits on a
# line of its own between them. This is the same limit the C# pass ran into
# with ShareX's correct root check, and it takes the same answer - the
# question moves from the statement to the whole method's text, and a method
# that compares a host anywhere in it is left alone.
#
# That is coarse. A method that checks one URL and loads another goes
# unreported, and quiet is the right direction to be coarse in.
#
# `URL(string:)` in the middle of the flow is not a sanitizer and is not
# listed as one. It parses, it does not judge, and a `javascript:` or a
# `file:` URL parses perfectly well.

[ "$$$U.fragment", "$$$U.queryItems", "$$$U.absoluteString",
  "$$$U.lastPathComponent", "$$$U.query", "UIPasteboard.general.string" ] as $untrusted
| [ "$$$V.load($R)", "$$$V.load($R, $$$_)",
    "$$$V.loadHTMLString($R, $$$_)",
    "$$$V.loadRequest($R)" ] as $loads
| ["func $F() { $$$BODY }"] as $methods
| "\\.\\s*host\\b[^\\n]*(?:==|hasSuffix|contains|hasPrefix)"
  + "|(?:==|hasSuffix|contains|hasPrefix)[^\\n]*\\.\\s*host\\b" as $comparesTheHost
| scan_ast("*.swift"; $untrusted + $loads + $methods) as $all
| ( $all | of($loads) | focus("R")
    | reaching($all | of($untrusted); [])
    | within($all | of($methods) | where_capture_not("BODY"; $comparesTheHost)) )
| finding("swift-webview-loads-untrusted-url";
    "whoever sent the app this URL chooses the page that renders inside it, "
    + "with the app's cookies and without an address bar; compare the host "
    + "against an allowlist first")
| report
